# Line endings.
#
# Ordinary sources normalise to LF in the repository and check out natively.
* text=auto

# ...but files whose SHA-256 is RECORDED must be byte-identical on every
# platform, so git must never translate them.
#
# On 2026-08-15 the R CMD check matrix caught this on Windows and nowhere else:
#
#   Error: [validate_urps_artifact] counts CSV SHA-256 does not match the manifest.
#   Error: [use_urps_artifact] artifact failed validation; the previous source
#          is unchanged.
#
# Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true, so every LF in these CSVs
# became CRLF on checkout, every byte count changed, and every recorded digest
# stopped matching. Verified: the manifest's digest matches the LF bytes and
# not the CRLF bytes.
#
# The consequence was not cosmetic. mufflyaccess is the cross-repo SSOT, and
# this made the canonical URPS artifact UNVALIDATABLE on Windows -- any Windows
# consumer got "artifact failed validation" and fell back to whatever source it
# already had. It was invisible for as long as CI ran on Linux alone.
#
# -text disables end-of-line conversion in both directions.
inst/extdata/** -text
tests/testthat/fixtures/** -text
*.parquet binary
*.rds binary
